## Original Content
Founded in 2001 to address regional security concerns, the SCO has evolved into a broad-based organization covering security, economic cooperation, connectivity, digital development and cultural exchanges. Its 25th anniversary comes at a time when countries across the world are facing growing uncertainties, making regional cooperation and stability increasingly important.

## Summary
The Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) turns 25, having expanded from a security-focused group to a multi-faceted organization covering economy, connectivity, digital development, and culture, amidst a backdrop of global uncertainties. Founded in 2001, it now emphasizes regional cooperation and stability. The SCO's evolution highlights its growing importance in addressing modern challenges.

## Key Points
- SCO was founded in 2001 primarily for regional security concerns
- Organization has broadened scope to include economic cooperation, connectivity, digital development, and cultural exchanges
- 25th anniversary coincides with heightened global need for regional cooperation and stability


